{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>It is not like the land of Egypt</b> — rather, it is better than it, and this promise was spoken to Israel at their departure from Egypt, for they were saying: perhaps we will not come to a land as good and beautiful as this one. Now, one might think the verse speaks in disparagement of it, thus saying to them: it is not like the land of Egypt — rather, it is worse than it. Scripture therefore teaches: \"and Hebron was built seven years before Zoan\" (Numbers 13:22) — one man built them; the way of the world is that a man first builds the fine structure and afterward the inferior one, etc. — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Deuteronomy 11:10), from the Sifrei (Ekev 11). And he further brought what they expounded in the Gemara in tractate Ketubot (Ketubot 112a) regarding another matter: it is possible that a man builds a house for his younger son and afterward for his older son; rather, one of the seven was built in Zoan. But the plain sense of the verse is stated by way of admonition: he said to them, \"And you shall keep all the commandment, and you shall possess a land flowing with milk and honey, for YHWH will give the rain of your land in its season, and the land will yield its produce\" — but know that it is not like the land of Egypt, to be watered by the foot, from the rivers and pools, like a vegetable garden; rather, it is a land of mountains and valleys, it drinks water from the rain of the heavens — not in another sense. And it requires that YHWH seek it out constantly with rain, for it is a very thirsty land and needs rain all year round; and if you transgress the will of YHWH and He does not seek it out with rains of favor, then it is very bad — you will neither sow nor will it sprout, and no grass will grow in its hills. And he will go back and explain all of this in the second passage (below, verses 13–17): \"if you diligently heed My commandments, I will give the rain of your land in its season, the former rain and the latter rain, continually; and if you do not heed… and He shuts up the heavens,\" etc., \"and you will perish quickly from the good land\" — for you will not be able to live in it without rain. Now, this passage admonishes concerning the way of the world, and from it we learn that even though all is in His hand and it is easy in the eyes of HaShem, may He be blessed, to destroy the inhabitants of the land of Egypt and to dry up their rivers and streams, still the land of Canaan will perish more quickly, when He does not give therein the rains of His might — the sick person needs merit and prayer that HaShem heal him more than the healthy person upon whom illness has not come, and so is the measure with the poor man and the rich man, and HaShem enlightens the eyes of both. And since he said (Deuteronomy 11:12), \"a land which YHWH your Elohim seeks out,\" and it would be fitting to say, \"it drinks water from the rain of the heavens, as YHWH your Elohim seeks it out,\" the midrash of our Rabbis (Sifrei Ekev 12) will be alluded to in the verse — for does He not seek out all lands, as it is written (Job 38:26), \"to cause it to rain on a land where no man is\"? As it were, He seeks out only it, and through that seeking with which He seeks it out, He seeks out all lands. \"The eyes of YHWH your Elohim are always upon it,\" to see what it needs and to renew therein decrees — times for good and times for evil, etc., as is found in tractate Rosh HaShanah (17b). And there is in it a profound secret, for this land is sought out in the All, and it is the All, and all the lands are sustained from it in truth."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The phrase 'one of the seven was built in Zoan' (משבעה אחד בצוען) is rendered hyper-literally; the reference is to the seven cities of the Anakites, with Hebron (the finest) built first and Zoan (inferior) among them."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:48:12.360114566Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}